# Pairs with NoKeyLost. Bounds the extent of the split/resize interlock: an
# adaptive split is refused only while a resize is in flight and is allowed on
# the resized copy during the completed resize's soft-delete window (the rule
# first proposed for #4452). The old copy still mirrors index-for-index into
# the resized copy and a saga stays bound to it (#4369), so a split that moves
# k2 to s2 on the resized copy takes the mirrored prepare onward, but the
# terminal the bound saga sends after the split has committed reaches only the
# resized copy's s1. The s2 bucket is never resolved, and once the registry
# forgets the saga it reads as a revert of an acknowledged commit.
MODULE: NoKeyLostSplitInSoftDeleteWindow
TARGET: NoKeyLost
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: a split on the resized copy during the soft-delete window strands the bound saga's bucket on the split target
PERTURBS: SplitBegin

--- FIND
SplitBegin ==
    /\ sp = "idle"
    /\ rs = "migrating" \/ rz \in {"idle", "purged", "undone"}
--- REPLACE
SplitBegin ==
    /\ sp = "idle"
\* MUTATION: the interlock covers only a resize in flight, not its soft-delete window.
    /\ rs = "migrating" \/ rz \notin {"snap", "copied", "swapped", "undoing"}
--- END
